a_renamed_global_reads_as_written_in_the_kernel.vyrn:6:0: `log` may not be returned — it is module state, which nothing may take, and a return is owned
  fix: `log.copy()` — the caller releases what it is handed
a_renamed_global_reads_as_written_in_the_kernel.vyrn:9:0: `a` may not be stored into module state `log` — it is a `read` parameter
  fix: declare the parameter `a: consume ..` if this function should own it
  fix: `a.copy()` if both sides need a value
a_renamed_global_reads_as_written_in_the_kernel.vyrn:12:0: `log` is written here while `t` still reads out of it
line 13: ... and `t` is used again here
  fix: `log.copy()` on line 11, so `t` is a value of its own
a_renamed_global_reads_as_written_in_the_kernel.vyrn:14:0: module state `log` may not be passed to a `consume` parameter via `take(..)` — nothing may take ownership of module state (it lives for the whole module and is never dropped)
a_renamed_global_reads_as_written_in_the_kernel.vyrn:15:0: `log` is written here while `log` still reads out of it
line 15: ... and `log` is read by `swap(..)` again here
  fix: `log.copy()` on line 15, so `log` is a value of its own
